@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "koroneiki"

Feature: Koroneiki Worker Contact and Entitlement API
	Testing Koroneiki Worker Contact and Entitlement API functionality.

Teardown:
	* I tear down the contact entitlement definitions on koroneiki with the following name values
	| Entitlement Name  |
	| Entitlement Name1 |
	| Entitlement Name2 |
	* I tear down the products on koroneiki with the following names
	| Liferay Digital Experience Platform |
	| Liferay Portal Six                  |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Koroneiki Automotive  |
	| Koroneiki Engineering |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contact roles on koroneiki with the following names
	| Default Account Worker Role  |
	| Optional Account Worker Role |

Scenario: Create contact entitlement
	Koroneiki worker contact entitlements should be able to be created.

	Given I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORAUTO                              | |
	| Description           | Test automotive account on koroneiki | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         | |
	| Name                  | Koroneiki Automotive                 | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         | |
	| Region                | United States                        | |
	| Status                | Active                               | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                   | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikiautomotive.com          | |
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default worker role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Worker Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Worker                               |
	And I assign worker contacts with the following email addresses to the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	| koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Koroneiki Automotive" to the following roles	
	| Default Account Worker Role |
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | Liferay Digital Experience Platform | |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" and the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}   |                |
	| Perpetual               | true               |                |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp1    | propertyValue1 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp2    | propertyValue2 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp3    | propertyValue3 |
	| Quantity                | 1                  |                |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate} |                |
	And I create a contact entitlement definition related to the product purchase of the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" and contact role with the name "Default Account Worker Role" and type "Account Worker" with the following values
	| Description | Entitlement Description |
	| Name        | Entitlement Name        |
	| Status      | Approved                |
	Then the contact entitlement definition with the name "Entitlement Name" should be present with the following values
	| Description | Entitlement Description |
	| Name        | Entitlement Name        |
	| Status      | Approved                |
	And the contact entitlement definition with the name "Entitlement Name" should be present via the entitlement definition key with the following values
	| Description | Entitlement Description |
	| Name        | Entitlement Name        |
	| Status      | Approved                |
	When I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Entitlement Name"
	And I create a nested field for the contact entitlement coming from the entitlement definition "Entitlement Name"
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the following values
	| Email Address            | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Entitlement Nested Field | ${staticContactEntitlementsNestedField}  |
	| First Name               | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language                 | English                                  |
	| Last Name                | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name              | User                                     |
	And the entitlement from the entitlement definition "Entitlement Name" should be visible via nested field on the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken"

Scenario: Create contact entitlement and view via uuid
	Koroneiki worker contact entitlements should be able to be created and viewed in a contact nested field via the uuid.

	Given I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORAUTO                              | |
	| Description           | Test automotive account on koroneiki | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         | |
	| Name                  | Koroneiki Automotive                 | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         | |
	| Region                | United States                        | |
	| Status                | Active                               | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                   | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikiautomotive.com          | |
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default worker role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Worker Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Worker                               |
	And I assign worker contacts with the following email addresses to the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	| koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Koroneiki Automotive" to the following roles	
	| Default Account Worker Role |
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | Liferay Digital Experience Platform | |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" and the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}   |                |
	| Perpetual               | true               |                |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp1    | propertyValue1 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp2    | propertyValue2 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp3    | propertyValue3 |
	| Quantity                | 1                  |                |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate} |                |
	And I create a contact entitlement definition related to the product purchase of the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" and contact role with the name "Default Account Worker Role" and type "Account Worker" with the following values
	| Description | Entitlement Description |
	| Name        | Entitlement Name        |
	| Status      | Approved                |
	Then the contact entitlement definition with the name "Entitlement Name" should be present with the following values
	| Description | Entitlement Description |
	| Name        | Entitlement Name        |
	| Status      | Approved                |
	And the contact entitlement definition with the name "Entitlement Name" should be present via the entitlement definition key with the following values
	| Description | Entitlement Description |
	| Name        | Entitlement Name        |
	| Status      | Approved                |
	When I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Entitlement Name"
	And I create a nested field for the contact entitlement coming from the entitlement definition "Entitlement Name"
	ThenI should be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" via uuid and the following values
	| Email Address            | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Entitlement Nested Field | ${staticContactEntitlementsNestedField}  |
	| First Name               | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language                 | English                                  |
	| Last Name                | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name              | User                                     |
	And the entitlement from the entitlement definition "Entitlement Name" should be visible via nested field on the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken"

Scenario: Create contact entitlement for worker contact with role only
	Koroneiki contact entitlements should be able to be created only for worker contacts with relevant roles.

	Given I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORAUTO                              | |
	| Description           | Test automotive account on koroneiki | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         | |
	| Name                  | Koroneiki Automotive                 | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         | |
	| Region                | United States                        | |
	| Status                | Active                               | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                   | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikiautomotive.com          | |
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact2                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default worker role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Worker Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Worker                               |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the optional worker role for accounts |
	| Name        | Optional Account Worker Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Worker                                |
	And I assign worker contacts with the following email addresses to the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	| koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Koroneiki Automotive" to the following roles	
	| Default Account Worker Role |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Koroneiki Automotive" to the following roles	
	| Optional Account Worker Role |
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | Liferay Digital Experience Platform | |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" and the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}   |                |
	| Perpetual               | true               |                |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp1    | propertyValue1 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp2    | propertyValue2 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp3    | propertyValue3 |
	| Quantity                | 1                  |                |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate} |                |
	And I create a contact entitlement definition related to the product purchase of the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" and contact role with the name "Default Account Worker Role" and type "Account Worker" with the following values
	| Description | Entitlement Description |
	| Name        | Entitlement Name        |
	| Status      | Approved                |
	Then the contact entitlement definition with the name "Entitlement Name" should be present with the following values
	| Description | Entitlement Description |
	| Name        | Entitlement Name        |
	| Status      | Approved                |
	And the contact entitlement definition with the name "Entitlement Name" should be present via the entitlement definition key with the following values
	| Description | Entitlement Description |
	| Name        | Entitlement Name        |
	| Status      | Approved                |
	When I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Entitlement Name"
	And I create a nested field for the contact entitlement coming from the entitlement definition "Entitlement Name"
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the following values
	| Email Address            | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Entitlement Nested Field | ${staticContactEntitlementsNestedField}  |
	| First Name               | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language                 | English                                  |
	| Last Name                | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name              | User                                     |
	And the entitlement from the entitlement definition "Entitlement Name" should be visible via nested field on the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	And the entitlement from the entitlement definition "Entitlement Name" should not be visible via nested field on the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken"

